# Legacy Neovim config removed in the lazy.nvim/Lua migration. These lived in
# ~/.config/nvim before the config moved to init.lua + lua/. chezmoi never
# deletes files just because they left the source tree, so list them here.
# Safe to drop once every machine has applied the migration.
# NOTE: after/ is intentionally not listed anymore — it's a managed directory
# again (after/ftplugin/{csv,tsv}.lua). Listing it here collided with the source
# dir and produced a chezmoi "inconsistent state (…, remove)" error.
.config/nvim/init.vim
.config/nvim/plugin
.config/nvim/ftdetect

# OpenCode V1 -> V2 migration. The skill moved to skills/ (V2's preferred
# location; the old skill/ would otherwise be discovered too and double-register
# the review-board skill), the git tool became plugins/git.ts (the old
# tools/git.ts uses the V1 plugin API and won't run on V2), and tui.jsonc was
# replaced by cli.json. chezmoi doesn't delete files that leave the source tree,
# so list the stale target paths here. Safe to drop once every machine applied.
.config/opencode/skill
.config/opencode/tools
.config/opencode/tui.jsonc
